  "The harness runs synthetic uniform codes, scales and activations; its FP64 comparison measures rounding, not model quality.",
  "The role corpus has 89 cases and eight redaction controls, so one flipped control moves the pass rate by 0.125. The two samples of the route differ from each other by as much as the earlier precision variants differ from production (redaction pass rate 0.500 and 0.625, critical misses 10 and 12); at this size the corpus cannot separate the route's quality from production's.",
  "Outputs differ, so decode tok/s mixes the round saving with each build's MTP acceptance on its own text: with no prompt the candidate accepted 0.423 of drafts against 0.461 and needed 113 rounds instead of 107, so decode moved +0.11% while each round was 5.4% shorter. Round time is the controlled metric.",
  "The profile gates ran once on the candidate. Its decode_2048 rate (167.68 tok/s against v0.8.1's receipted 151.33) is one sample on its own text, and its 130,048-token wall (60.4 s against 59.1 s) runs prefill kernels the route does not change.",
  "RTX 5090 only: the route is compiled out for sm_86 and sm_89, and the RTX 4090 lane was not measured.",
  "The profiled 26K round (16.65 -> 15.55 ms) overstates the saving; unprofiled A/B/B/A rounds moved 16.01 -> 15.24 ms. Unchanged Q4 kernels next to the rerouted projections also shortened in graph (GDN query/key -0.22 ms, MLP gate/up -0.11 ms per round)."
